--TEST--
a `#[Core\Route]` attribute answers its card and then every grant the `nvs.toml` beside the file gives the whole program, `rule:ide/a-route-hover-shows-the-programs-grants`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class ShopController {
    #[Core\Ro<|>ute(method: Core\Http\Method::Get, path: "/items")]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    public function items(): string {
        return "";
    }
}
--FILE nvs.toml--
[capabilities.fs]
read = ["./data"]

[capabilities.net]
connect = ["api.example.com"]

[capabilities.db]
connect = ["main"]
--FILE data/x.txt--
x
--REQUEST--
hover
--EXPECT--
```nvs
#[Core\Route(path: string, method: Core\Http\Method, name?: string, slotted?: bool)]
```

Declares the HTTP path and method this method handles. Write it twice to handle two methods.

Written above a method.

---

These are the grants of the whole program, from `nvs.toml`. Every route of the program has the same grants.

- `fs.read`: `data`
- `fs.write`: only the directories `Core\IO::temporaryDir` makes (default)
- `script.spawn`: files in this file's directory, outside its temporary directories (default)
- `net.connect`: `api.example.com`
- `db.connect`: `main`

No other grant is given.
